{
	title: 'Modal overlays in the terminal',
	spec: 'Modal UI (model picker, /login, /config, find) draws over the conversation instead of replacing whole rows: the frame is composited, so the transcript stays visible left and right of the box, with one blank column and an outline around it, and the diff renderer handles it like any other frame change. A modal has a fixed height: 80% of the rows, at most 50, and scrolls its contents, so typing into a search box never makes it jump. Modals are client-only and never in history; their result is an ordinary command. See tasks/w4/forms.md (Modals) and tasks/cc/terminal.md.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Shape: src/common/modals.ts holds ModalState { title, hint?, form?, items, selected, scroll } and modals.step(state, key) -> { state, action: submit { answers, item? } | cancel }: up/down move through items, Enter submits, Escape cancels, every other key goes to forms.step on the form (the search box); an edit resets selected and scroll to 0. modals.scroll(scroll, selected, count, visible) is minimal-motion scrolling.',
		'Terminal: frame.build(view, cols, rows) composites view.modal via frame.withModal (box from frame.modalBox: fixed height, width 80% of cols capped at 100, centred on the writable screen, so it never touches scrollback). Rows right of the box are cut with strings.sliceVisual, which replays the escapes active at the cut. The frame reports modalScroll and render.draw writes it back into view.modal.scroll: the list keeps its place between frames only because the view holds app.state.modal by reference.',
		'App: app.open(modal, submit) opens a modal over everything (it takes keys before an open question and the prompt); Enter closes it and sends submit(action) if that returns a command; Escape only closes it (it never pauses the session). app.close() closes it from outside.',
		'Web: not built. kv was terminal-only by its title; the model picker (0x) must add the web side, using modals.step for keys and a DOM box (a native <dialog> is the lazy choice).',
		'For 0x (model picker): open it with app.open(modals.open({ title, hint, form: one text field \'search\', items })) on Ctrl-M and /model. Refiltering is not built: after each modals.step whose search value changed, recompute items (ranked) from the host\'s model list, e.g. an optional `change(state) -> state` hook next to submit in app.open. Items are plain strings (cleaned and clipped by the frame); map `action.item` back to your ranked list to build the switch command. Ctrl-M is legacy Enter (\\r); only the kitty protocol (on by default, CSI 109;5u) tells them apart, so check keys.ts decodes ctrl+m as { key: \'m\', ctrl: true } and that app routes it before prompt.apply. The current model line and a thinking level belong in the form (forms.md): the level field type does not exist yet.'
	],
	needs: ['cc', 'w4']
}
